Now write the test script. I'll make it log each step and assert. Use `page.evaluate` with functions.

Important: `page.evaluate` serializes return values; objects with Set not serializable, so return plain.

Helper for dialogs:
```
async function dialog() {
 return page.evaluate(()=>({
  open: document.querySelector('#dialogShade').classList.contains('open'),
  title: document.querySelector('#dialogTitle').textContent,
  text: document.querySelector('#dialogText').textContent,
  choices:[...document.querySelectorAll('#dialogChoices button')].map(b=>b.textContent)
 }));
}
async function clickChoice(needle){
 const found = await page.evaluate((needle)=>{
   const btns=[...document.querySelectorAll('#dialogChoices button')];
   const b=btns.find(b=>b.textContent.includes(needle));
   if(!b)return false; b.click(); return true;
 }, needle);
 if(!found) throw new Error('choice not found: '+needle+' in '+JSON.stringify(await dialog()));
 await page.waitForTimeout(100);
}
```
Clicks via DOM bypass actual UI but exercise handlers. Good.

`waitFor` with `page.waitForFunction`.

Teleport and interact:
```
async function interactAt(x,y){ await page.evaluate(([x,y])=>{__game.player.x=x;__game.player.y=y;},[x,y]); await page.evaluate(()=>__game.interact()); await page.waitForTimeout(50); }
```
Note: `player.awake` must be true. After opening click, yes.

For task flow, set girls speed=200 and mood=100 at start to reduce waiting. But `speed` affects only NPCs; `moveActor` uses g.speed. We'll set. Also set history=2.

However, high speed may cause them to overshoot? moveActor step min(d, speed*...*dt), so no overshoot. Good.

Breakfast test:
```
await page.evaluate(()=>{__game.girls.filter(g=>!g.dog).forEach(g=>{g.speed=200;g.mood=85;g.history=2});});
await interactAt(495,560);
// callGirls executed. Some may refuse.
let statuses=...
for each refusing: for attempts call redirectGirl
await page.waitForFunction(()=>__game.girls.filter(g=>!g.dog).every(g=>g.seatedAtTable), {timeout:20000});
```
But `redirectGirl` sets destination; if girl was refusing, good. If `callGirls` had a girl wandering (not refusing), redirectGirl also works. If callStatus coming, no need.

Then `interactAt(495,560)`; expect dialog "Handle Make breakfast". Click "I’ll handle it."; wait tasks.breakfast.

Potential issue: Dad at table and seated girls nearby; `interact` picks nearbyGirl (close) and `found` table. Condition nearbyGirl && currentCallTask && status refusing/wandering. After all seated, statuses 'arrived', so no. Fine.

After breakfast complete, `postMealTimer=2.5`; wait 3s so girls get up and routes clear.

Showers:
- Interact at (90,520). `handleShowerInteraction` opens dialog with choices "Call Elaina first", etc. Choose first. Then dialog showerParenting. Click calm. If dialog still open and title contains "Call X for a shower", click calm again. Loop:
```
for (let i=0;i<12;i++){
 const d=await dialog();
 if(!d.open) break;
 if(d.title.startsWith('Call ')) await clickChoice('Let’s talk it through together');
 else if(d.title==='Showers, one at a time') await clickChoice('Call Elaina first');
 else break;
}
