But after success, `showerParenting`'s choice run calls sendGirlToTask, then the outer dialog handler closes. Good.
- Wait for showerIndex===1 (Elaina finished) with timeout 20s. But note `showerOrder` includes [Elaina, Elsie, Ellerle] based on girls order. If we choose Elaina first. Then `showerIndex` increments when she arrives.
- Interact at shower station again -> `handleShowerInteraction` opens dialog for next girl (Elsie). It doesn't show choices? It calls `showerParenting(next)` directly. So dialog title "Call Elsie for a shower". Click calm until success. Wait showerIndex===2.
- Repeat for Ellerle. After third, completeTask('showers'), tasks.showers true.
- Note `handleShowerInteraction` may return early if `next.callStatus==='showering'||routeMode==='shower'`; after first arrives, callStatus='showered', routeMode='', so fine.
- If respond fails and we retry, `showerParenting` opens a new dialog each time. Fine.

Laundry:
- Interact at washer (190,520). `openLaundryDialog` title "Wash & dry the laundry". Click "I’ll handle the laundry."; wait tasks.laundry after 7s. Test.
- Then maybe test delegation on lunch? Not necessary, but we should test `requestLaundryHelp` flow at least once. Could reset tasks.laundry=false and washTimer=0, call `__game.openLaundryDialog()`, click "Ask a girl to help…", choose "Elsie", click calm until success, check washTimer>0 and girl routeMode calledTask. Then wait tasks.laundry. But this resets task and repeats. We can do it before final completion. Let's do:
  - Reset tasks.laundry=false.
  - Call interact at washer; click "Ask a girl to help…"; dialog "Laundry delegation" choices names; click "Elsie"; dialog "Talk with Elsie"; click calm; if fail, dialog reopens (requestLaundryHelp). Loop until washTimer>0. Then wait 7s tasks.laundry.
